# Trusted roots for http_request (verify_ssl: true). The device trusts ONLY
# these, instead of the built-in public CA bundle:
#
#   hw.airgradient.com   AirGradient cloud upload. Uses AirGradient's private
#                        CA (not in any public store), pinned here the same
#                        way AirGradient's own firmware does.
#   luukvisser.github.io Update manifest and firmware. Let's Encrypt chain
#                        (YR1 -> Root YR, cross-signed by ISRG Root X1).
#
# ISRG Root X2 and DigiCert Global Root G2 are backups in case GitHub Pages
# moves to Let's Encrypt's ECDSA chain or another CA; without them, update
# checks would stop and devices would need a dashboard/USB flash to recover.
#
# Before each release, check both hosts still chain to a root in this file:
#   openssl s_client -connect <host>:443 -servername <host> -showcerts </dev/null
# Review before 2032 (expiry of the Root YR cross-sign).
#
# Root                                SHA-256 fingerprint                                                                              Expires
# AirGradient Sensor Labs Root CA     64:9A:DF:2F:2F:0F:42:E5:CC:D8:39:B7:7A:B1:EC:18:19:D5:94:5F:7B:4E:7F:08:9C:F8:CA:E9:D0:81:37:AE 2041-09-12
# ISRG Root X1                        96:BC:EC:06:26:49:76:F3:74:60:77:9A:CF:28:C5:A7:CF:E8:A3:C0:AA:E1:1A:8F:FC:EE:05:C0:BD:DF:08:C6 2035-06-04
# ISRG Root X2                        69:72:9B:8E:15:A8:6E:FC:17:7A:57:AF:B7:17:1D:FC:64:AD:D2:8C:2F:CA:8C:F1:50:7E:34:45:3C:CB:14:70 2040-09-17
